        <item>
            <title>2.0</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 12:31:55 +0700</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,system-ui,sans-serif;margin:0;padding:0 4px}h2{font-size:20px;margin:6px 0 4px}h3{font-size:13px;margin:16px 0 4px}p{margin:4px 0}.date{opacity:.6}ul{margin:4px 0;padding-left:20px}li{margin:4px 0}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}</style></head><body><h2>2.0</h2><p class="date">Release date: 5 Oct 2026</p><h3>New in 2.0</h3><ul><li>Works on Windows and Linux through the Claude Code mod – one license for the app and the mod.</li><li>The bell in the panel footer shows what needs you: a chat waiting for your reply, an agent spending tokens fast, a skill description that's too long. Open the chat where it runs – Antigravity, VS Code or its Terminal tab – or mute what you don't need.</li><li>Every row on the main screen opens a popover now: what it is, where it's stored, tokens per call and where it ran.</li><li>While Claude Code works, the app uses 5% CPU instead of 13%, with peaks of 30% instead of 90%.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
